{"id": 7, "ts": 1779490132.975113, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I\u2019d like to add two observations from my interview that bear on the crew\u2011cooperation and communication criteria. Candidate\u202fC repeatedly emphasized crew welfare, describing concrete situations where he deliberately deferred to a co\u2011pilot\u2019s judgment or took extra steps to ensure others\u2019 safety\u2014behaviour that supports a strong collaborative attitude. He also demonstrated excellent attention to detail in the simulator, catching subtle checklist items that others missed, reinforcing his reliability and information\u2011accuracy.\nThat said, there is a tension between this collaborative stance and the dossier\u2019s note that he is perceived as egocentric; my interview did not reveal overt self\u2011promotion, so the perception may stem from communication style rather than intent. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB\u2019s stress resilience is solid, but his \u201cwrong tone\u201d and pretentiousness could impair cockpit communication, while Candidate\u202fA\u2019s unfriendly demeanor and Candidate\u202fD\u2019s moody, loner traits raise concerns for crew dynamics.\nTo resolve the remaining uncertainty, I suggest we seek any additional evidence on Candidate\u202fC\u2019s communication style in operational settings (e.g., reference checks or behavioural interview excerpts) before finalising our recommendation.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_3\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}"}
